														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3688391">
									

<p>While I sincerely enjoyed this SCP, and I upvoted it, there's a lot of writing issues, e.g. proofreading and style issues, with it. I'll point out some of the ones I saw, but there's a lot that could be improved.</p>
<p>1. &quot;The newly selected Class-D personnel is to be inoculated with a very small explosive charge of remote activation inside thoracic chamber prior their entry. &quot; Inoculated refers to vaccines. You probably meant injected. &quot;of remote activation&quot; is very strange. Better would be &quot;that can be remotely activated.&quot;</p>
<p>2. &quot;the need to rotate the Class-D personnel has been deemed null as long as the previous procedures are being followed.&quot; &quot;has been deemed null&quot; is strange - null isn't used that way. &quot;Null&quot; could be replaced by &quot;unnecessary&quot;.</p>
<p>3.&quot;The current observed radius outside SCP-3509 for this effect to take place are 5. ██ meters.&quot; &quot;are&quot; should be &quot;is&quot;</p>
<p>4. &quot;Any attempts to breach the underground complex by any other means have ended on failure.&quot; &quot;on&quot; should be &quot;in&quot;.</p>
<p>5. &quot;intern hemorrhage.&quot; &quot;intern&quot; should be &quot;internal&quot;</p>
<p>Also, the writing could be much more clinical in a number of places. I'd be happy to go in to more detail if you're interested.</p>
<p>This is a really good SCP idea, and it will be a very good SCP with some polishing. My favorite part was the realization of why the Junior Researcher committed suicide rather than tap dance.</p>

							</div>

								
